🛡️ Garuda Infrastructure Progress Report
Date: August 3, 2026

Project: Garuda — Multi-Agent AI Governance & Execution Platform

Authors: Garuda Core Engineering Team

1. Executive Summary
Over the recent engineering cycles, the Garuda Core Gateway and storage engine underwent major platform enhancements. The system evolved from basic decision management to a cryptographically verifiable, self-governing multi-agent platform.

We implemented:

Model Context Protocol (MCP) integration for dynamic tool discovery.

Autonomous Contradiction Quarantine Engine to catch and isolate conflicting multi-agent decisions in real-time.

Token Budget Metering & Pre-Flight Ledger to prevent runaway agent execution costs.

Cryptographic Evidence Chain & Merkle Verification providing O(1) linear verification and O(logN) inclusion proofs for tamper-evident decision auditing.

2. Technical Breakdown: What We Built
A. Autonomous Contradiction Quarantine Engine
Purpose: Detect conflicting policy decisions created across distributed multi-agent workflows.

Mechanism: When an agent submits a decision to a specific (scope_domain, scope_system) pair, the engine queries existing decisions in that scope. If a contradiction is detected, the new decision is marked with status: "quarantined" and quarantined: true, and a contradiction_id record is saved for governance review.

B. Real-Time Token Budget Metering
Purpose: Enforce pre-flight budget checks and token usage tracking for agent requests.

Mechanism: Evaluates token balance prior to request execution and writes usage entries to an append-only ledger post-execution.

C. Cryptographic Evidence Chain & Merkle Verification
Purpose: Provide tamper-evident, non-repudiable proof of decision lineage and evidence artifacts.

Mechanism:

Computes deterministic SHA-256 leaf hashes from decision payloads.

Chains leaf hashes to the previous tenant Merkle root (ChainHash(parent_root, leaf_hash)).

Persists updated Merkle roots atomically using Postgres row locks (FOR UPDATE).

Exposes an attestation API (GET /api/v1/evidence/verify/{decision_id}) returning leaf_hash, parent_hash, root_hash, block_height, and verification status.

3. Key Issues Faced & How We Fixed Them
Issue / Error Code	Root Cause	Resolution / Fix
Cascade Quarantine False Positives	GetDecisionsByScope queried decisions without filtering out already quarantined decisions, causing subsequent proposals in a scope to perpetually conflict with old drafts.	Updated DetectAndQuarantine in internal/engine/contradiction.go to explicitly skip decisions with status == "quarantined" or status == "superseded".
SQLSTATE 42703 (Column does not exist)	Code queries attempted to insert into domain / system or scope_domain / scope_system before schema unification.	Created migration 013_add_scope_columns.sql adding scope_domain and scope_system to decisions, and synchronized flat struct fields with nested types.Scope.
SQLSTATE 42P10 (ON CONFLICT constraint mismatch)	PostgreSQL ON CONFLICT (id) failed because the table primary key was either missing or set as a compound key (tenant_id, id).	Created migration 014_fix_decisions_primary_key.sql setting PRIMARY KEY (tenant_id, id) and updated upsert queries to ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, id) DO UPDATE.
pgx.ErrNoRows on First Submission	First decision for a new tenant failed because GetMerkleRoot could not find an existing root and threw driver-level empty set errors.	Updated GetMerkleRoot in internal/store/merkle_store.go to check for sql.ErrNoRows and strings.Contains(err.Error(), "no rows"), automatically triggering createGenesisMerkleRoot.
types.DecisionStore missing method build error	GetDecisionRevisions was omitted during a refactor of decision_store.go, breaking interface compliance across cmd/garuda-api and cmd/garuda-mcp.	Restored GetDecisionRevisions signature and implementation in internal/store/decision_store.go.
