🛡️ Garuda Architecture Specification (GAS) & Engineering Progress Report
Date: August 3, 2026
System: Garuda — Organizational Intelligence Runtime
Target Standard: Garuda Architecture Specification (GAS) Roadmap & Architectural Principles
1. Executive Summary & Strategic Positioning
Garuda is built not as an AI chatbot or a model-centric orchestration framework, but as an Organizational Intelligence Runtime. Its core mandate is to separate enduring organizational intelligence from interchangeable foundation models—keeping models as replaceable compute engines while preserving truth, memory, reasoning, governance, and learning in a persistent, append-only semantic substrate.
To satisfy the Garuda Architecture Specification (GAS) laws, all platform primitives must be deterministic, explainable, append-only, and fully replayable. Recent engineering cycles focused on solidifying the Layer 0 (Truth Foundation), Layer 1 (Directed Truth Graph), and Layer 7 (Intent Governance / Merkle Verification) subsystems.
