A. Autonomous Contradiction Quarantine Engine (Layer 0 / Layer 1 / Layer 7)
GAS Alignment: Fulfills GAS Volume 001 (Canonical Object Model) and Volume 005 (Canonical Semantic Model) by enforcing semantic validation prior to canonical knowledge promotion.
Functionality: When an agent proposes a decision for a (scope_domain, scope_system) pair, the engine queries existing active decisions in PostgreSQL. If a semantic contradiction is detected, the decision is flagged as status: "quarantined" and quarantined: true, and an audit contradiction_id record is saved for governance review.
B. Real-Time Token Budget Metering (Layer 0)
GAS Alignment: Fulfills GAS Volume 001 (Budget Primitive) and Volume 007 (Runtime Resource Scheduling).
Functionality: Performs pre-flight budget checks before executing agent requests and logs token consumption into an append-only ledger post-execution.
C. Cryptographic Evidence Chain & Merkle Verification (Layer 0 / Layer 7 / GAS Vol 009 & 011)
GAS Alignment: Implements GAS Volume 009 (Persistence & Temporal Semantics) and Volume 011 (External Contracts). Enforces the core invariant: Truth is append-only and cryptographically non-repudiable.
Functionality:
Generates deterministic SHA-256 leaf hashes from decision payloads.
Chains leaf hashes to the previous tenant Merkle root (ChainHash(parent_root, leaf_hash)).
Atomically persists updated Merkle roots in PostgreSQL using row-level locking (FOR UPDATE).
Exposes an attestation API (GET /api/v1/evidence/verify/{decision_id}) returning leaf_hash, parent_hash, root_hash, block_height, and "is_verified": true.
3. Engineering Incident Resolution Log (Issues & Fixes)
During the integration of the Cryptographic Merkle Verification subsystem, several database constraint, schema, and driver edge cases were identified and resolved:
Issue / Error Code
Root Cause
Solution / Architectural Fix
Cascade Quarantine False Positives
GetDecisionsByScope queried decisions without filtering out already quarantined decisions, causing subsequent proposals in a scope to perpetually conflict with old drafts.
Updated DetectAndQuarantine in internal/engine/contradiction.go to explicitly skip decisions with status == "quarantined" or status == "superseded".
SQLSTATE 42703 (Column scope_domain missing)
Database schema previously stored scope using individual or composite column names that differed from the Go domain struct fields.
Applied migration 013_add_scope_columns.sql adding scope_domain and scope_system to decisions, and updated Go store structs to maintain fallback sync between nested Scope structs and flat table fields.
SQLSTATE 42P10 (ON CONFLICT constraint mismatch)
PostgreSQL ON CONFLICT (id) failed because decisions used a compound primary key (tenant_id, id) or lacked an explicit single-column primary key constraint.
Applied migration 014_fix_decisions_primary_key.sql setting PRIMARY KEY (tenant_id, id) and updated store upsert queries to ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, id) DO UPDATE.
pgx.ErrNoRows on Initial Decision
First decision for a new tenant failed because GetMerkleRoot encountered an empty result set and threw driver-level empty set errors.
Updated GetMerkleRoot in internal/store/merkle_store.go to check for sql.ErrNoRows and strings.Contains(err.Error(), "no rows"), automatically triggering createGenesisMerkleRoot.
Interface Compliance Compiler Error
GetDecisionRevisions was accidentally omitted during a store refactor, violating the types.DecisionStore interface across cmd/garuda-api and cmd/garuda-mcp.
Restored GetDecisionRevisions in internal/store/decision_store.go matching the types.DecisionStore interface signature.

